"""Question banks for the simple games on the shadow site (17 Nov 2026).

Each entry: (answer, map, clue, [two wrong answers], tier, fact)
  tier 1 = warm-up (most people know it), 2 = think about it, 3 = the clever one.
  The day's ten are 4 + 3 + 3. Aim: an average player scores about 7.
  The wrong answers set the difficulty as much as the question: warm-ups get easy-to-rule-out
  options, clever ones get close neighbours.
  'map' is a view name for that game (a continent, the UK, or a country code).
Every answer is checked against the full game's own data when the tool runs.
"""

